### The tutorials of the editor window: the card, the menu and the steps.

menu-help-tutorials = Tutorials
tutorial-label = Tutorial
tutorial-count = Step { $step } of { $count }
tutorial-show-me = Show me
tutorial-skip = Skip the step
tutorial-end = End
tutorial-done = Done
tutorial-finished = Done
tutorial-finished-text = You did each step of this tutorial. Help → Tutorials has the others.

## Your first scene.

tutorial-first-scene-title = Your first scene
tutorial-first-scene-add = Add an empty entity: right-click an empty part of the hierarchy and choose Add an empty entity.
tutorial-first-scene-name = Press F2 (or double-click the row) and name the new entity Lamp.
tutorial-first-scene-light = In the inspector, type light in Add component… and choose Light.
tutorial-first-scene-place = Set the Y of Transform → Position to 2, so the lamp hangs above the floor.
tutorial-first-scene-save = Press ⌘S to save the scene.

## A prefab.

tutorial-prefab-title = Make a prefab
tutorial-prefab-select = Select an entity in the hierarchy or in the Scene view.
tutorial-prefab-make = Choose Entity → Make a prefab of the selection. The entity becomes an instance of a new prefab file.
tutorial-prefab-copy = With the instance selected, press ⌘D: the copy uses the same prefab file.
tutorial-prefab-save = Press ⌘S to save the scene.

## A sequence.

tutorial-sequence-title = Animate with a sequence
tutorial-sequence-new = Choose Sequence → New sequence and name it intro. The window opens the new sequence.
tutorial-sequence-select = Select the entity to animate in the hierarchy or in the Scene view.
tutorial-sequence-key = In the inspector, press the key mark beside Position: the sequence keeps the place of the entity at this time.
tutorial-sequence-second = Move the time of the Timeline to 2 s, move the entity, and press the key mark again.
tutorial-sequence-play = Press Space to play the sequence.
